{
  "info": {
    "name": "API Platform Demo",
    "description": "Two demo APIs on the WSO2 API Platform Gateway, both JWT-protected with org identity read from the verified org_name claim (not a header). Folder 1: OrderManagementAPI (claim-based dynamic routing + token exchange). Folder 2: AgentChatAPI (claim-based, per-org AND per-org-per-use-case token-based rate limiting).\n\nGet a token by running '1a' (Railco) or '1b' (Acme) -- each uses that org's own client_credentials application and saves into the shared {{access_token}} variable. NOTE: the IS instance's TLS cert is expired/self-signed -- in Postman go to Settings > General and turn OFF 'SSL certificate verification' globally, otherwise the token requests will fail with a TLS error.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "gateway_base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "railco_is_base_url", "value": "https://localhost:9444" },
    { "key": "railco_client_id", "value": "REPLACE_WITH_RAILCO_CLIENT_ID" },
    { "key": "railco_client_secret", "value": "REPLACE_WITH_RAILCO_CLIENT_SECRET" },
    { "key": "acme_is_base_url", "value": "https://localhost:9444" },
    { "key": "acme_client_id", "value": "REPLACE_WITH_ACME_CLIENT_ID" },
    { "key": "acme_client_secret", "value": "REPLACE_WITH_ACME_CLIENT_SECRET" },
    { "key": "access_token", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. OrderManagementAPI - Dynamic Routing",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1a. Generate Token - Railco (Client Credentials)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.access_token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"access_token\", jsonData.access_token);",
                  "    console.log(\"Saved Railco access_token to collection variable.\");",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.error(\"No access_token in response:\", jsonData);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"Response has access_token\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.access_token).to.exist;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{railco_client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{railco_client_secret}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "client_credentials", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{railco_is_base_url}}/oauth2/token",
              "host": ["{{railco_is_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token"]
            },
            "description": "Requests an application-level access token using Railco's own OAuth2 application (its own client_id/client_secret, and its own token endpoint via {{railco_is_base_url}} in case Railco is served by a different IS instance/tenant than Acme). Fill in railco_client_id / railco_client_secret / railco_is_base_url in the collection variables first. On success, the test script saves access_token into the {{access_token}} collection variable, ready for the AgentChatAPI/OrderManagementAPI requests below -- assuming this application's own org_name claim resolves to \"Railco\" on this IS."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1b. Generate Token - Acme (Client Credentials)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.access_token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"access_token\", jsonData.access_token);",
                  "    console.log(\"Saved Acme access_token to collection variable.\");",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.error(\"No access_token in response:\", jsonData);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"Response has access_token\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.access_token).to.exist;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{acme_client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{acme_client_secret}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "client_credentials", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{acme_is_base_url}}/oauth2/token",
              "host": ["{{acme_is_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token"]
            },
            "description": "Requests an application-level access token using Acme's own OAuth2 application (its own client_id/client_secret, and its own token endpoint via {{acme_is_base_url}} in case Acme is served by a different IS instance/tenant than Railco). Fill in acme_client_id / acme_client_secret / acme_is_base_url in the collection variables first. On success, the test script saves access_token into the {{access_token}} collection variable, ready for the AgentChatAPI/OrderManagementAPI requests below -- assuming this application's own org_name claim resolves to \"Acme\" on this IS."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Invoke OrderManagementAPI",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Request completed\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 502, 503]);",
                  "});",
                  "console.log(\"Status:\", pm.response.code, pm.response.status);",
                  "console.log(\"Body:\", pm.response.text());"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                { "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway_base_url}}/order-management/v1.0/orders",
              "host": ["{{gateway_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["order-management", "v1.0", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "Calls OrderManagementAPI-v1.0 using the token saved above. jwt-auth verifies the token, then dynamic-routing reads org_name from the verified claim and routes to the matching upstreamDefinitions entry (\"Railco\" or \"Acme\"). A token whose org claim doesn't match either name returns 502/503 by design (no fallback map configured)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. AgentChatAPI - Token Rate Limiting",
      "description": "Requires a token whose org_name claim is Railco or Acme -- run folder 1's request 1a (Railco) or 1b (Acme) first. Current Railco limits: org=500/min, usecase1=200/min, usecase2=100/min. Each call costs 50 tokens (mock-agent-backend.js returns a fixed X-Completion-Tokens: 50).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Railco usecase1 (run 5x -- 1-4 succeed, 5th blocked at 429)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "console.log(\"Status:\", pm.response.code);",
                  "console.log(\"x-ratelimit-remaining:\", pm.response.headers.get(\"x-ratelimit-remaining\"));",
                  "console.log(\"x-ratelimit-quota:\", pm.response.headers.get(\"x-ratelimit-quota\"));",
                  "console.log(\"Body:\", pm.response.text());"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Use-Case-Id", "value": "usecase1" }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [ { "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" } ]
            },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway_base_url}}/agent/v1.0/chat/completions",
              "host": ["{{gateway_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["agent", "v1.0", "chat", "completions"]
            },
            "description": "Consumes railco-usecase1-token-budget (200/min) AND railco-org-token-budget (500/min) simultaneously, since org quota has no use-case filter and matches every Railco call. At 50 tokens/call: usecase1 alone allows 4 calls before the 5th is blocked (429, x-ratelimit-quota: railco-usecase1-token-budget) -- click Send 5 times in a row to see it happen."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Railco usecase2 (run 3x -- 1-2 succeed, 3rd blocked at 429)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "console.log(\"Status:\", pm.response.code);",
                  "console.log(\"x-ratelimit-remaining:\", pm.response.headers.get(\"x-ratelimit-remaining\"));",
                  "console.log(\"x-ratelimit-quota:\", pm.response.headers.get(\"x-ratelimit-quota\"));",
                  "console.log(\"Body:\", pm.response.text());"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Use-Case-Id", "value": "usecase2" }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [ { "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" } ]
            },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway_base_url}}/agent/v1.0/chat/completions",
              "host": ["{{gateway_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["agent", "v1.0", "chat", "completions"]
            },
            "description": "Consumes railco-usecase2-token-budget (100/min) AND railco-org-token-budget simultaneously. At 50 tokens/call: usecase2 alone allows 2 calls before the 3rd is blocked (429, x-ratelimit-quota: railco-usecase2-token-budget) -- click Send 3 times in a row to see it happen. After running this AND request 1 above to full exhaustion, the org budget has consumed 200 (usecase1) + 100 (usecase2) = 300 of its 500 total -- 200 still remaining, proven by request 3 below."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Railco org quota STILL has room (different use-case, after 1+2 exhausted)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Org quota still had room -- 200 even though usecase1/usecase2 are individually exhausted\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200);",
                  "});",
                  "console.log(\"Status:\", pm.response.code);",
                  "console.log(\"x-ratelimit-remaining:\", pm.response.headers.get(\"x-ratelimit-remaining\"));",
                  "console.log(\"x-ratelimit-quota:\", pm.response.headers.get(\"x-ratelimit-quota\"));",
                  "console.log(\"Body:\", pm.response.text());"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Use-Case-Id", "value": "usecase-onboarding" }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [ { "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" } ]
            },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway_base_url}}/agent/v1.0/chat/completions",
              "host": ["{{gateway_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["agent", "v1.0", "chat", "completions"]
            },
            "description": "THE DEMO POINT: X-Use-Case-Id here is \"usecase-onboarding\" -- a use-case with NO dedicated quota configured, so only railco-org-token-budget (500/min) applies to this call, not any per-use-case limit. Run this AFTER exhausting requests 1 and 2 above (usecase1 and usecase2 both individually blocked at 429). This call still succeeds with 200, proving the org-wide budget still has room (500 - 200 - 100 = 200 remaining) even though both specific use-case quotas are maxed out -- org and use-case budgets are independent, and a 3rd/other use-case is only ever gated by the org-wide ceiling."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
